# Example Vaultwarden render map for Bazarr. Values are never stored in Git.
# Format: ENV_NAME|folder|item|field
#
# Render these to a local Bazarr config reference before deploy. Bazarr does not
# consume these as Docker env vars; it stores Sonarr/Radarr connection settings
# (including their API keys) and the OpenSubtitles credentials inside its own
# config DB under /config. This map exists so the deploy card knows exactly which
# Vaultwarden items must exist and be rendered/entered at provision time.
#
# OpenSubtitles.com account + API key — HUMAN-FETCHED credential. Neither the
# design, implementation, nor automation can invent it; Ben must supply it.
# The deploy card treats the absence of this item as a hard block.
OPENSUBTITLES_USERNAME|homelab|bazarr/opensubtitles|username
OPENSUBTITLES_API_KEY|homelab|bazarr/opensubtitles|api_key
#
# Sonarr (TV) connection — API key from live config.xml <ApiKey>.
SONARR_API_KEY|homelab|sonarr/service|api_key
#
# Radarr (movies) connection — API key from live config.xml <ApiKey>.
RADARR_API_KEY|homelab|radarr/service|api_key